The distinction between elastic and plastic behavior depends on conditions.
The same material can respond differently at different stresses, temperatures, and loading conditions;
steel can deform elastically under smaller loads and undergo plastic deformation after reaching the relevant yield conditions, where permanent deformation begins.

In industrial processing, a press applies high pressure to steel parts so that they undergo plastic deformation and retain their new shape.
This example describes material processing;
a single stress value cannot define a common boundary for all steels.

